      "nets": [
        "GND"
      ],
      "observed": "The netlist places SKW92A pins 13 and 14, labeled LAN_PORT3_TX+ and LAN_PORT3_TX-, directly on the GND net.",
      "expected": "Unused Ethernet PHY differential pairs should not be tied directly to ground; the specification describes the Ethernet PHY nets in the reference netlist as single-node/unconnected, and standard practice is to leave unused differential PHY pins open or terminate them according to the datasheet rather than shorting them to ground.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX+\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"14\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX-\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "the RJ45 jack `J5`'s data pads ... all appear in the netlist as individually unconnected, while the `LAN1_RX+/-`, `LAN1_TX+/-` global labels used elsewhere resolve to single-node nets containing only `U5` (SKW92A) pins."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "This shorts the port-3 transmit differential pair to ground and to each other, potentially loading or damaging the Ethernet PHY and causing the board to behave differently from the intended design.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files show a likely anomaly: SKW92A Ethernet PHY pins 13 and 14 are tied directly to GND, whereas the intended/reference behavior leaves unused Ethernet PHY nets single-node/unconnected rather than shorting differential signal pins to ground."
}

